.TH GOFMT 1
.SH NAME
gofmt \- format Go source code
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gofmt
.RI [ flags ]
.RI [ path ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B gofmt
reads Go source code and emits the canonical formatting defined by the
installed Go release. With no paths it reads standard input. A path may name a
file or a directory tree.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-d
Display a diff instead of formatted source.
.TP
.B \-e
Report all parse errors.
.TP
.B \-l
List files whose formatting differs.
.TP
.BI \-r " rule"
Apply a rewrite rule before formatting.
.TP
.B \-s
Apply permitted source simplifications.
.TP
.B \-w
Write the formatted result back to each source file.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR go (1)
